--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/input-compatibility.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# EIS input compatibility and tested limits
+
+The EIS compatibility patch requires libeis 1.6 because it handles `EIS_EVENT_SEAT_DEVICE_REQUESTED`. It advertises buttons and scrolling on the absolute pointer, sets a valid physical scale, and converts v120 discrete scrolling to Wayland wheel steps without reversing the sign. Virtual keyboard events update xkb modifier state using the same keymap sent to the compositor.
+
+Desktop bounds include every output instead of the first one. The accepted hardware test used two adjacent 1920×1080 monitors at scale 1, configured before the bridge started. This is not a complete logical-output implementation: fractional or mixed scaling, rotation, output removal and EIS region renegotiation after hotplug still need work. Restart the bridge after changing monitor geometry. Do not describe these changes as general multi-monitor or keyboard-layout support.
